  "notes": "{見受|みう}ける is a formal verb most commonly used in the passive form {見受|みう}けられる. It expresses a polite or indirect way of saying something was noticed or observed.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: Xが{見受|みう}けられる (passive, most common)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {見受|みう}けられている means \"has been observed\" (resulting state)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜が{見受|みう}けられる (something is observed/noticed)\n- 〜と{見受|みう}けられる (it appears that...)\n- 〜{様子|ようす}が{見受|みう}けられる (signs of... are observed)\n\nThis verb is primarily used in written or formal spoken Japanese. In casual speech, {見|み}える or {気|き}づく are more natural.",
